    "modifiedAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "rdt_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -324
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Topographic reaction\n\nA three-stage pipeline. 1 · Gray–Scott reaction–diffusion (the Simulation node's `reaction` mode) grows from a few seed blobs; hold the mouse to paint more chemical into it. 2 · Contours reads the chemical picture as terrain (its `image` mode): filled bands for the elevation tints and finer isolines on top. 3 · Paper: film grain, like a printed survey map.\n\n• Drag on the canvas: paint.  • Bang: start over.  • Toggle: the raw chemicals instead of the map.\n• Presets panel: Coral, Maze, Spots, Fingerprints (the reaction's `preset`).\n• Slider into `levels`: how many contour bands.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 260
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Topographic reaction\n\nA three-stage pipeline. 1 · Gray–Scott reaction–diffusion (the Simulation node's `reaction` mode) grows from a few seed blobs; hold the mouse to paint more chemical into it. 2 · Contours reads the chemical picture as terrain (its `image` mode): filled bands for the elevation tints and finer isolines on top. 3 · Paper: film grain, like a printed survey map.\n\n• Drag on the canvas: paint.  • Bang: start over.  • Toggle: the raw chemicals instead of the map.\n• Presets panel: Coral, Maze, Spots, Fingerprints (the reaction's `preset`).\n• Slider into `levels`: how many contour bands.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
